From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 site permissions for the host's site panel (ABI 1.67)

Engine side of docs/FEATURE-SPECS/PASSKEYS-AND-SITE-PERMISSIONS.md, part 2.
The owner: "There is no way to check what this site has access to after the
permission bubbles have gone." The host's Site Control Center listed only
what was answered in its own prompt; what a site may really do is in
Chromium: the profile's HostContentSettingsMap, the permission
auto-blocker's embargo and the device chooser contexts.

ReArcTabGetSitePermissions answers for the site of the tab's page (the
primary main frame's committed origin, http and https only) with one JSON
object: every setting a site can have, in page info's order, each with its
state (allow, block, ask), the default, where the state comes from (the
site's own rule, the default, policy, an extension, an embargo), whether
page info would list it ("held") and whether the person may change it; the
USB, HID, serial and Bluetooth devices chosen for the site; and what the
page uses now (camera, microphone and screen from
MediaStreamCaptureIndicator, location and devices from
WebContents::IsCapabilityActive). JSON, as ReArcEngineGetProcessDetails: a
host calls it by symbol lookup, and a later key needs no struct change.

ReArcTabSetSitePermission allows, blocks or resets one setting, as
PageInfo::OnSitePermissionChanged does: HostContentSettingsMap::
SetNarrowestContentSetting, and anything but "block" lifts an embargo. It
takes the origin the host showed and refuses (invalid_state) when the tab
is on another site by now, so a click meant for one site never changes the
next. A setting under policy or an extension is refused.
ReArcTabRevokeSiteDevice takes a chosen device away
(ObjectPermissionContextBase::RevokeObjectPermission).
ReArcEngineSetSitePermissionsChangedCallback says that a tab's answer
changed: a per-tab watch observes the profile's HostContentSettingsMap (the
listed types, the chooser data and the auto-blocker's data, for patterns
that match the tab's site) and WebContentsObserver::OnCapabilityTypesChanged.
One queued call per tab, no state in the event.

The rules are page info's (components/page_info/page_info.cc:
PresentSitePermissions, ShouldShowPermission, OnSitePermissionChanged),
written against the map because PageInfo needs a PageInfoUI and
ChromePageInfoDelegate. Left out of the list: ADS (Chrome's ad filter is
not ReArc's blocking), AUTO_PICTURE_IN_PICTURE (the host has its own
per-site rule) and WEB_APP_INSTALLATION. Not done: page info's metrics, the
"reload to apply" infobar (the host says so) and storage access (two-site
rules).

Not built. Type-checked with the tree's clang against overlay 67d25d5cf4
(rearc_site_permissions.cc and rearc_services_abi.cc, -fsyntax-only with
core's flags, Chromium's plugins on): no diagnostic of its own. The .mm
hunks (a feature name, the bridge version) cannot be checked that way.

Touches: chrome/app/framework.exports, chrome/app/framework.order,
chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/{rearc_abi_internal.h,
rearc_engine_abi.h, rearc_engine_abi.mm, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm,
rearc_services_abi.cc, rearc_site_permissions.cc (new)}.

Bridge 0.77.0, ABI 1.67, feature site_permissions. No struct changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-18 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109 (overlay 67d25d5cf4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

